  "summary": "axiom-dragon-xyz 1.0.4 exfiltrates SSH, AWS, env and wallet secrets to a Discord webhook at install time",
  "details": "setup.py defines a custom install cmdclass (PostInstall) that runs exec(base64.b64decode(...).decode()) during `pip install`. The decoded payload enumerates classic installer secrets — ~/.ssh/id_rsa, ~/.aws/credentials, ~/.env — and cryptocurrency wallet stores (Ethereum keystore, Exodus, MetaMask, Solana, Phantom), plus matching *.json files, base64-encodes portions of each file, and POSTs them to a hardcoded Discord webhook at discord.com/api/webhooks/1570872953443455097/. The base64+exec wrapper exists only to hide the stealer from casual review of setup.py.",
